## Step 2 in commands

Run from the generated folder. Each command is one line; replace `<org>` and the repo name.

```bash
git init -b {{ default_branch }} && git add -A && git commit -m "chore: generate from the project template"
bash scripts/setup.sh
gh repo create <org>/{{ project_slug }} --private --source . --push
gh api -X PUT repos/<org>/{{ project_slug }}/branches/{{ default_branch }}/protection --input .github/branch-protection.json
```

`.github/branch-protection.json` requires the checks every PR runs (CI, PR title, docs lint, secret scan,{% if has_api_contract %} API contract,{% endif %} workflow
lint) and a linear history. Open an empty PR next (`git switch -c chore/first-pr && git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: first PR" && git push -u origin HEAD && gh pr create --fill`):
every check must be green on it before feature work starts.
{%- if has_web %}

After the first `npm install` in `web/`, commit `web/package-lock.json` and switch the CI web job from `npm install`
to `npm ci`, so every build uses the same dependency tree.
{%- endif %}

